                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi WZW
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(\mathcal{L}_{WZW})
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping"} looping
                  of the class of the Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle.
          %p
            We discuss now how this construction generalizes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            in general, and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+supergeometry"} higher supergeometry
            in particular. Then in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#TheBraneBouquet"} The brane bouquet of higher super WZW terms
            we discuss a class of examples of this construction arising from the tower of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ extensions
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS13b"} FSS 13b
